I ascended role 11 of 13, a gnomish ranger, on NAO a couple of days
ago. Wish I'd had time to complete this one during the June
tournament, as it extended my winning streak to four. Real life has
kept me (pleasantly) busy however, so I played this one slowly over a
couple of weeks, and don't remember a lot of details.

Lots of altars, including a co-aligned temple, an embarrassing number
of magic lamps (six or seven, I think), a bones pile including two
such lamps, speed boots, and a bathtub full of holy water, really
helped out this ranger. Playing a gnome meant I started out with
crossbow, which I decided to keep despite not being able to train the
skill for the Longbow. Gnomish Mines sure were a lot friendlier,
though I forgot my race and committed cannibalism once, granting me
permanent aggravate monster - oops. Sokoban had the bag for the third
time in a row when I already had one and wanted the amulet. At least I
had GDSM from a magic lamp in Minetown, and another lamp got me an
amulet of reflection soon enough. (I didn't want to depend exclusively
on the Longbow's reflection, which only works while wielded.) A
randomly generated +5 dwarvish helm also helped out a lot. I already
had an AC below -20 by the time I went on my quest.

Learned a lot of spells, and found I could cast magic missile at 0%
failure even with that helm and a small shield. So I used that in
preference to the Longbow, though I did gather over 150 arrows,
rustproof and enchant them to +6. I had fun in Rodney's tower when I
decided to take out the monsters in the zoo with the bow; rust monster
ate the arrows and "spit them out in disgust"! Unfortunately this
removed the rustproofing, but it didn't matter as I had plenty to
spare and post-Rodney I wasn't going to be using the bow anyway.

Used Mjollnir at first when it was granted, then after being crowned
Vorpal Blade primarily, switching to MagicBane for curse avoidance in
the endgame. I hadn't used Vorpy in awhile, preferring the greater
damage of Frosty when I can get it, but did enjoy the 10% beheading
chance; especially nice luck when Yeenoghu showed up. Also fun to
instantly slay jabberwocks.

Had a couple of pets, including a pit fiend for a long while, who
eventually got killed by a trapper in the Valley. I posted separately
about my pet purple worm who leveled up to 45 swallowing wraiths, then
got slimed. Gave up on pets after that, and did Gehennom alone. Though
I hadn't found several parts of my ascension kit (and never found a
wand for polypiling), I was impatient to finish, and magic-mapped as
much as possible (too bad I only had scrolls, not a spell), wishing
for what was missing as I found more magic lamps. Used a luxury wish
on a helm of brilliance so I could get cure sickness down to 0%.

Elemental planes were very easy. One of the adventurers on Astral had
Frost Brand; I was of a mind to take it from him, but didn't want him
to freeze any more of my full healing potions in combat, so I
teleported him out of the way. Second altar was the right one, and I
offered for my 12th NAO victory, 11th class ascended. Only Knight and
Samurai left to go.

